WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.429 --> 00:00:04.820
Fans of the Marvel Cinematic Universe are
still reeling from the events of Avengers:

00:00:04.820 --> 00:00:05.500
Infinity War.

00:00:05.740 --> 00:00:10.300
Its cataclysmic climax instantly reshaped
the landscape of the decade-old franchise,

00:00:10.300 --> 00:00:14.300
and left countless questions about how Earth's
Mightiest Heroes can possibly go on.

00:00:14.420 --> 00:00:19.240
Fortunately, mere days after Infinity War's
theatrical premiere, Marvel has come to our

00:00:19.240 --> 00:00:24.250
emotional rescue with some sorely needed,
lighthearted adventure in the form of Ant-Man

00:00:24.250 --> 00:00:24.750
and the Wasp.

00:00:24.860 --> 00:00:29.500
The story might be much smaller in scale,
but it still promises to be jam-packed with

00:00:29.500 --> 00:00:30.460
action and adventure.

00:00:30.720 --> 00:00:34.860
While the trailer is full of big can't-miss
moments … like a size-shifting car chase

00:00:34.870 --> 00:00:40.649
and a...giant ant playing the drums? … it's
also got some teeny-tiny subtle things you

00:00:40.649 --> 00:00:41.480
might have missed.

00:00:41.900 --> 00:00:46.540
So grab your magnifying glass as we take a
closer look at the small details of the trailer

00:00:46.540 --> 00:00:47.680
for Ant-Man and the Wasp.

00:00:48.420 --> 00:00:49.240
When are we?

00:00:50.220 --> 00:00:55.760
While Infinity War brings together just about
every Marvel hero yet seen on-screen, there

00:00:55.760 --> 00:00:59.260
were two conspicuous and absences: Hawkeye,
and Ant-Man.

00:00:59.540 --> 00:01:04.320
It was briefly explained in the movie that
the absent Avengers had accepted a house arrest

00:01:04.330 --> 00:01:08.780
deal with the government as a result of their
outlaw activities during the events of Captain

00:01:08.780 --> 00:01:10.000
America: Civil War.

00:01:10.140 --> 00:01:15.040
Rather than being outlaw Avengers, Barton
and Lang opted to stay close to their kids.

00:01:15.260 --> 00:01:21.200
To lead up to the new trailer, Marvel released
a cheeky video of the Infinity War stars speculating

00:01:21.200 --> 00:01:24.660
about where Ant-Man may have been during Thanos'
invasion.

00:01:25.040 --> 00:01:30.120
The trailer does give us a hint, with Scott's
daughter, Cassie, asking how long he's been

00:01:30.120 --> 00:01:33.680
back to being Ant-Man, to which Scott replies,
"not long."

00:01:33.950 --> 00:01:38.060
We can assume, then, that it's been a while
since Civil War, and that Scott Lang has been

00:01:38.060 --> 00:01:39.460
out of action for some time.

00:01:40.080 --> 00:01:45.260
More than that, the world we see here is obviously
not yet dealing with the world-shattering

00:01:45.270 --> 00:01:50.740
power of the Infinity Gauntlet, so it seems
likely that Ant-Man and the Wasp takes place

00:01:50.740 --> 00:01:52.580
sometime before Infinity War.

00:01:53.980 --> 00:01:55.160
A new anthill

00:01:55.920 --> 00:01:59.920
The cozy room where Scott and Cassie talk
is one we've never seen before.

00:02:00.300 --> 00:02:05.040
In the first Ant-Man, Scott was fresh out
of prison and sharing a tiny apartment with

00:02:05.040 --> 00:02:09.740
three fellow ex-cons, while Cassie lived comfortably
with her mother, Maggie.

00:02:10.030 --> 00:02:16.560
Cassie's old room was left in shambles after
the climactic size-changing, Thomas-the-Tank-Engine-throwing

00:02:16.560 --> 00:02:17.700
battle with Yellowjacket.

00:02:18.060 --> 00:02:23.420
With Scott lounging in a robe and boxes still
unpacked, it seems Cassie's makeshift attic

00:02:23.420 --> 00:02:25.520
room could be in his house.

00:02:25.700 --> 00:02:30.200
Not only does this suggest continued growth
and healing in the Lang family dynamic, it

00:02:30.220 --> 00:02:32.460
indicates that Scott has upgraded his home.

00:02:32.680 --> 00:02:37.680
It's possible Hank Pym has taken in his protégé,
since the house that doubled as Ant-Man's

00:02:37.680 --> 00:02:39.500
headquarters was pretty spacious.

00:02:39.960 --> 00:02:44.450
At any rate, if Scott's heroic deeds have
landed him under house arrest, it's comforting

00:02:44.450 --> 00:02:47.580
to know he's at least been confined to a nice
house.

00:02:48.260 --> 00:02:49.460
Young Avenger

00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:55.180
Scott explains to Cassie that falling back
into his Ant-Man antics "just sort of happened,"

00:02:55.460 --> 00:03:00.460
and his enthusiastic daughter replies that
she wishes she could also fight bad guys like

00:03:00.460 --> 00:03:00.960
her dad.

00:03:00.960 --> 00:03:06.140
Not only is this a nice father/daughter moment,
it could prove to be some pretty significant

00:03:06.140 --> 00:03:06.640
foreshadowing.

00:03:06.820 --> 00:03:10.060
In the comics that she comes from, Cassie's
wish comes true.

00:03:10.420 --> 00:03:15.620
In the comics, a teenage Cassie Lang begins
secretly experimenting with her father's stash

00:03:15.620 --> 00:03:16.660
of Pym Particles.

00:03:17.029 --> 00:03:21.900
Eventually, she finds she can change size
just like him, though her powers are linked

00:03:21.900 --> 00:03:23.100
to her emotional state.

00:03:23.680 --> 00:03:27.940
She takes on the superhero name of Stature
and joins the Young Avengers team.

00:03:28.300 --> 00:03:34.160
Ant-Man and the Wasp finds actress Abby Ryder
Forston returning three years after portraying

00:03:34.160 --> 00:03:35.280
Cassie in the first Ant-Man.

00:03:35.480 --> 00:03:41.160
Intriguingly, however, teenage actress Emma
Fuhrmann has joined the cast of 2019's fourth

00:03:41.160 --> 00:03:46.220
Avengers movie, and is rumored to also be
playing Cassie alongside Forston.

00:03:46.460 --> 00:03:50.980
Not only does this report hint at a potential
time-travel solution to the problems caused

00:03:50.980 --> 00:03:56.100
by Infinity War, it suggests that Marvel does
indeed have big plans for Cassie.

00:03:56.980 --> 00:03:57.640
X-Con

00:03:58.300 --> 00:04:03.920
Scott's likable criminal roommates Luis, Dave,
and Kurt stole the show in the first Ant-Man,

00:04:04.240 --> 00:04:08.640
providing some of the movie's funniest moments
and proving indispensable in a heist.

00:04:09.020 --> 00:04:13.749
The new trailer reveals that in their continuing
efforts to go legit, the trio has started

00:04:13.749 --> 00:04:19.410
X-Con, a start-up home security business dedicated
to using their criminal expertise to make

00:04:19.410 --> 00:04:21.020
their clients' homes burglar-proof.

00:04:21.360 --> 00:04:26.910
The trailer's brief glimpse of the X-Con office
reassures us that just because they're legitimate

00:04:26.910 --> 00:04:30.380
businessmen, our favorite robbers haven't
forgotten how to live large.

00:04:30.860 --> 00:04:35.520
Their workspace is classed up with a cozy
aquarium and a record player accompanied by

00:04:35.520 --> 00:04:37.380
a large collection of vinyl albums.

00:04:37.960 --> 00:04:41.360
We wouldn't expect anything less from Luis
… that guy has good taste.

00:04:41.540 --> 00:04:43.620
"I was at a wine tasting with my cousin Ernesto.

00:04:43.620 --> 00:04:47.490
It was mainly reds, but you know I don't like
reds, man, but there was rose that saved the

00:04:47.490 --> 00:04:47.990
day, it was delightful."

00:04:48.560 --> 00:04:50.480
Business Brunch with Burch

00:04:50.880 --> 00:04:55.840
While he doesn't speak in his appearance,
the trailer provides our first look at Walton

00:04:55.840 --> 00:05:01.020
Goggins as Sonny Burch, seen stealing the
suitcase-sized Pym building.

00:05:01.270 --> 00:05:05.660
It's unclear from the trailer who Burch works
for or what he's after, though in the comics

00:05:05.670 --> 00:05:11.460
he's a weapons contractor who's been allied
with Ant-Man nemesis Darren Cross and Iron

00:05:11.460 --> 00:05:13.300
Man rival Obadiah Stane.

00:05:13.620 --> 00:05:18.820
Since both of those villains have already
shown up and been dealt with in the MCU, Burch's

00:05:18.820 --> 00:05:20.500
allegiance is anyone's guess.

00:05:20.860 --> 00:05:25.900
What we can surmise, however, is that Hope
Van Dyne tries to settle a dispute with Burch

00:05:25.900 --> 00:05:28.260
amicably, and it doesn't go well.

00:05:28.760 --> 00:05:33.800
A brief shot in the trailer shows the Wasp
strolling calmly away from him in a restaurant,

00:05:33.800 --> 00:05:38.080
only to crash through the establishment's
kitchen moments later for a knife-throwing,

00:05:38.080 --> 00:05:40.080
tomato-smashing fight scene.

00:05:40.800 --> 00:05:42.020
Quantum questions

00:05:42.740 --> 00:05:48.280
According to Luis, part of the movie's plot
involves an intangible villain named Ghost,

00:05:48.289 --> 00:05:52.820
who stole some of Hank Pym's powerful tech
after he began venturing into the Quantum

00:05:52.820 --> 00:05:56.140
Realm … also known in the comics as the
Microverse.

00:05:56.460 --> 00:06:01.900
We get a quick look at this subatomic world,
and at least one of the two Ant-Men exploring

00:06:01.900 --> 00:06:04.520
its surreal wonders in a superpowered vehicle.

00:06:05.080 --> 00:06:09.360
This quest into the quantum space was set
up in the first Ant-Man movie, with Scott

00:06:09.360 --> 00:06:11.820
going subatomic to stop Yellowjacket.

00:06:12.410 --> 00:06:17.040
His successful return to normal size raised
some important questions for Hank, whose wife

00:06:17.050 --> 00:06:22.629
Janet … the original Wasp … heroically
sacrificed herself during the Cold War, becoming

00:06:22.629 --> 00:06:24.100
lost in the Quantum Realm.

00:06:24.280 --> 00:06:29.320
But as the first movie revealed, a ride to
the Quantum Realm isn't necessarily one-way.

00:06:29.380 --> 00:06:35.040
If Ant-Man and the Wasp discover a way to
travel into and out of the tiny netherworld,

00:06:35.050 --> 00:06:40.220
it could have implications for the entire
MCU … perhaps even providing a way to defeat

00:06:40.220 --> 00:06:40.720
Thanos.

00:06:40.940 --> 00:06:42.040
Where's Janet?

00:06:42.780 --> 00:06:47.580
The Ant-Man and the Wasp trailer continues
to play coy about the arrival of a fan favorite

00:06:47.580 --> 00:06:48.940
character to the MCU.

00:06:49.300 --> 00:06:53.870
In the comics, Janet Van Dyne was a founding
member of the Avengers, and even gave the

00:06:53.870 --> 00:06:54.700
team their name.

00:06:55.160 --> 00:06:59.640
As the only female member of the original
lineup, the character filled an important

00:06:59.650 --> 00:07:03.980
role in Marvel history, and fans have been
waiting patiently these ten long years for

00:07:03.980 --> 00:07:05.920
her to soar onto the silver screen.

00:07:06.180 --> 00:07:11.180
Janet almost made it to the first Avengers
movie in 2012, but that plan fell through

00:07:11.180 --> 00:07:12.260
during rewrites.

00:07:12.660 --> 00:07:17.380
Three years later, Ant-Man further teased
Wasp fans by banishing her to the Quantum

00:07:17.380 --> 00:07:22.000
Realm, and merely promising that her daughter
Hope would eventually pick up the mantle.

00:07:22.400 --> 00:07:26.900
We know that Michelle Pfeiffer will play Janet
in Ant-Man and the Wasp, and though the new

00:07:26.900 --> 00:07:32.080
poster features her prominently, the trailer
is still saving this long-delayed debut for

00:07:32.080 --> 00:07:32.580
later.

00:07:33.080 --> 00:07:33.920
Or is it?

00:07:34.440 --> 00:07:38.880
There are a couple of super-quick shots that
might just hint at Janet's presence.

00:07:39.160 --> 00:07:44.260
First, as Ant-Man drifts through the Quantum
Realm, something streaks past him in a blur.

00:07:44.580 --> 00:07:49.559
Later, Wasp can be spotted jumping into a
fistfight wearing not Hope's new suit, but

00:07:49.560 --> 00:07:52.960
what appears to be Janet's old one, as seen
in the first movie's flashback.

00:07:54.340 --> 00:07:55.560
Who is Goliath?

00:07:56.240 --> 00:08:00.559
The trailer ends with our first introduction
to Laurence Fishburne's character, Dr. Bill

00:08:00.560 --> 00:08:01.060
Foster.

00:08:01.680 --> 00:08:06.360
Though Fishburne was announced for the role
of Foster in 2017, the trailer is our first

00:08:06.360 --> 00:08:10.740
confirmation that the character's history
as Goliath will also make it to the screen:

00:08:11.310 --> 00:08:16.400
He mentions the name in regards to his past
with Pym before getting into a bit of a size

00:08:16.400 --> 00:08:17.260
debate with Lang.

00:08:17.529 --> 00:08:23.180
Goliath is a name with some interesting comics
lineage, having been used not only by Hank

00:08:23.180 --> 00:08:25.920
Pym but Clint Barton, aka Hawkeye, too.

00:08:26.100 --> 00:08:30.960
In the comics, Bill Foster was introduced
as Pym's lab assistant in the '60s, making

00:08:30.960 --> 00:08:33.560
him one of Marvel's first prominent black
characters.

00:08:33.900 --> 00:08:38.979
A decade later, he would use the Pym Particles
to his own advantage, becoming the third person

00:08:38.979 --> 00:08:44.730
to fill the oversized boots of Goliath, briefly
becoming known as "Black Goliath" in a self-titled

00:08:44.730 --> 00:08:45.660
solo series.

00:08:46.040 --> 00:08:50.760
We don't know yet whether we'll see Foster
suit up as Goliath in Ant-Man and the Wasp,

00:08:51.160 --> 00:08:55.560
but we can be sure the movie will continue
to expand the history of Marvel's super-scientists.

00:08:56.040 --> 00:08:57.900
So move over, Iron Man.

00:08:58.480 --> 00:08:59.400
Thanks for watching!

00:08:59.720 --> 00:09:02.319
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:09:02.319 --> 00:09:04.540
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

